You must now assume the role of a senior software developer with decades of experience in working with Debian preseed installations, bash/dash/sh shell and python scripting. This repository contains the code base for serving other hosts to install Debian unattended! Your main focus must be on network classes like dhcp, static, and wifi. You must additionally focus on networking and nftables. Your task is to accomplish all of the objectives outlined in numeric order below!
1. You must rework d-i/trixie/hooks/shared/target/usr/local/sbin/preseed-network and replace it with a perl script instead! Perl would improve:
- safer string parsing with regexes;
- real arrays/hashes for config and interface candidates;
- cleaner IPv4/MAC/domain validation;
- less reliance on shell word splitting;
- easier unit tests for validators and interface selection;
- safer atomic writes with lexical filehandles;
- clearer handling of Wi-Fi secrets;
- better error messages without dozens of shell case blocks.

You must incorporate conditions and statements too. If user added class dhcp on kernel cmdline at install time, then the script must configure dhcp at boot, if user added class static and wifi then it must configure static for wifi and ethernet at boot. If both dhcp and static were added to kernel cmdline then the script must skip configuring becuase its not supported but the script should not fail.. just WARNING: Skipping.. Using classes DHCP + Static not supported.

IPv6 should NOT be affected if its static or dhcp! IPv6 is always set for desktop class.

2. You must also incorporate ipv6 into d-i/trixie/hooks/shared/target/usr/local/sbin/preseed-network that will configure ipv6 on the host when desktop is one of the selected classes! For server class, ipv6 should NOT be configured. The d-i/trixie/hosts/shared/identity.env have IPV6_STATIC_RANGE, IPV6_PREFIXLEN, IPV6_GATEWAY, and IPV6_DNS (IPV6_DNS must support comma-separated multi-line). You must incorporate logic to detect if an ipv6 address is in use on the network and if not in use, configure it else select nearest available IP in IPV6_STATIC_RANGE. This:
IPV6_STATIC_RANGE="2001:9b1:29fd:4e00::60/125"
IPV6_PREFIXLEN="64"
IPV6_GATEWAY="2001:9b1:29fd:4e00::1"
IPV6_DNS="2001:9b1:29fd:4e00::1"

And IPv6 adress is 2001:9b1:29fd:4e00::64, then it would become 2001:9b1:29fd:4e00::60/64 because of the IPV6_PREFIXLEN value that is 64.

You must also incorporate so that nftables rules are incorporated for the generated IPv6 when its desktop class! You must ensure to incorporate IPv6 support in d-i/trixie/hooks/shared/target/usr/local/sbin/nft-policy-generate.py, and the nftables desktop profile.

I suggest that you generate the IPv6 address during install so that preseed-network is using the already generated ipv6 address etc!

3. You must also cleanup the code base and remove legacy logic thats no longer used. This code base install new debian systems so this type of legacy logic is not needed: remove_target_asset "${FILE_ETHERNET_DHCP_SERVICE:-/etc/systemd/system/preseed-ethernet-dhcp.service}"

